<title>JAPAN: Tokyo money market closed for national holiday.</title>
<headline>Tokyo money market closed for national holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo money market is closed for national holiday on Monday. Trading will resume on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The weighted average of the key overnight call rate was 0.47 percent on Friday. Key three-month certificates of deposit (CD) were issued at 0.53 percent.</p>
<p>The settlement price of the benchmark March three-month Euroyen deposit rate futures was 99.18 on Friday.</p>
</text>
